  "summary": "Traditional Sami drinking vessels carved from birch burl, featuring distinctive shapes and sometimes decorative ornamentation.",
  "description": "Characterized by their rounded shape carved from birch burl, often with a raised rim and sometimes decorated with pewter thread or simple carving, these cups evolved from practical nomadic containers to objects of cultural significance. The tradition reflects the Sami relationship with the boreal forest and the importance of communal gatherings where these vessels were used.",
